Item 4 of #32 is stuck. Two issues are waiting on each other, so I asked the hub to decide and stopped. I made no commit this run, and the issue stays open with the `needs-decision` label.

Items 1–3 are already on main as `3422a79`. The manager merged them on the full gates, and build pipeline 3056431600 passed.

**The deadlock on item 4 (`ready = true` for the `test-idp` listener):**
- The hub decided on 2026-11-09 that item 4 waits until the NEG `seatrials-test-idp` exists. Nobody has commented yet that it does, and I can't check: this run has no gcloud credentials for `tacplus-dev`.
- Only the first test-idp run, in fleet-seatrials#27, creates that NEG.
- But fleet-seatrials#27 is marked `Blocked-by: tacplus-dev/cloud#32` (and also by cluster#17, which is still open). So it won't run again until this issue closes, and this issue can't close until that run creates the NEG.

**What I recommended** in my comment on the issue:
- Close #32 now, since items 1–3 are done, and move item 4 into its own issue that waits on fleet-seatrials#27.
- Remove `Blocked-by: tacplus-dev/cloud#32` from fleet-seatrials#27. It needs only items 1–3 to create the NEG, so it can run once cluster#17 lands.
- The alternative is to keep #32 open and remove that `Blocked-by` from fleet-seatrials#27 by hand.

I checkpointed the state to `looper/cloud-32`, so the next run acts on whichever the hub chooses.
